    "name": "Decaf RC Translation Drill",
    "text": "2\nDecaf RC Translation Drill\n≥ 1 SECTION\nInstructions\n\nNOTE: Do your recaps out loud in the beginning to keep yourself honest about the quality and completeness of the recaps. Transition to silent recaps when you feel like you're ready.\n\nRead, translate, and quip paragraph 1*. Do it just like LR.\n\nThis means all the details are included just like they would be on LR.\n\nQuip after every Translation. \n\nThis standard applies to every paragraph you ever translate on RC.\n\nLook away from paragraph 1 and recap the FULL TRANSLATION of paragraph 1 silently.\n\nThe recap is not a summary, gist, or main point.\n\nThe recap should not omit names, dates, and lists.\n\nThe recap should not be a shopping list of information. It should be a story in your own words.\n\nIt is encouraged to mix up the order of the sentences and ideas.\n\nThis standard applies to every paragraph (or collection of paragraphs) you ever recap on RC.\n\nRead, translate, and quip paragraph 2. Do it just like LR.\n\nLook away from paragraph 2 and recap the FULL TRANSLATION of paragraph 2 silently.\n\nWithout looking back, recap the Translations of paragraphs 1 + 2 back to back silently.\n\nRead, translate, and quip paragraph 3. Do it just like LR.\n\nLook away from paragraph 3 and recap the FULL TRANSLATION of paragraph 3 silently.\n\nWithout looking back, recap the Translations of paragraphs 1 + 2 + 3 back to back silently.\n\nRepeat this pattern for all remaining paragraphs.\n\nComplete this same process on all remaining passages in the section.\n\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
