anslate-x-[1px]\n          active:not-disabled:-translate-y-[1px]\n          active:not-disabled:shadow-[1px_1px_0_0_#171712]\n         h-[38px] gap-2 text-caption-medium border-[2px] !size-9.5 !gap-0 !px-0 -translate-x-[3px] -translate-y-[3px] shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#171712] \n          h-8! w-11.5! shrink-0!\n          group-hover/expandable:-translate-x-[3px]\n          group-hover/expandable:-translate-y-[3px]\n          group-hover/expandable:bg-soft-white\n          group-hover/expandable:shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#171712]\n          group-has-[[data-no-expand]:hover]/expandable:translate-x-0!\n          group-has-[[data-no-expand]:hover]/expandable:translate-y-0!\n          group-has-[[data-no-expand]:hover]/expandable:shadow-none!\n          peer-hover/bookmark:translate-x-0! peer-hover/bookmark:translate-y-0!\n          peer-hover/bookmark:shadow-none!\n          hover:-translate-x-[3px] hover:-translate-y-[3px] hover:bg-soft-white\n          hover:shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#171712]\n         \n            shrink-0 self-start\n            lg:h-11! lg:w-15.5\n          \" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Close view\" aria-expanded=\"true\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"transform: rotate(180deg);\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"21\" height=\"21\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-testid=\"lucide-chevron-down-icon\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></div></span></button></div><div class=\"\n          flex flex-col gap-2 px-4 pb-4\n          md:px-8 md:pb-6\n        \"><h4 class=\"text-body-l font-extrabold text-soft-black\">Instructions</h4><div class=\"prose text-body-s\"><ol>\n<li>\n<p>Every day, translate elevated reading material from outside the LSAT, using the following sources:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.sciencedaily.com/\" target=\"_blank\">ScienceDaily.com </a></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Ideal daily reading for those who feel alienated by scientific language or fear science passages in RC</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Be sure to choose the&nbsp;articles that challenge you the most, not articles that look familiar or interesting</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://aeon.co/\" target=\"_blank\">Aeon.co </a></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>The most similar articles to LSAT RC on the internet</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Reading an Aeon.co article every day is a great habit if you have no specific topic-based weaknesses, but would like to make RC-style reading a habit.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.aldaily.com/\" target=\"_blank\">ALDaily.com</a></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Ideal daily reading for those who feel alienated by abstract language, art, humanities, and pretension.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Be sure to choose the articles that look the most unfamiliar, not articles that speak to your pre-existing interests.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/York-Times-Guide-Essential-Knowledge-ebook/dp/B005EXS7E4/ref=tmm_kin_swatch_0\" target=\"_blank\">NYT Guide to Essential Knowledge</a></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>The single best way to fix gaps in common knowledge</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Here is a list of sections in the Guide that are relevant to LSAT. If any of these topics would trouble you as an RC passage, read over that section of the guide.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>LSAT Relevant Guide Sections</strong>: Architecture, Zoology, Botany, History, Art, Photography, Literature, Music (the serious parts about jazz and blues, especially), Film, Dance, Drama, Climate &amp; Weather and Glossary of Weather Words (In Geography), Government, Law, Philosophy, Biology, Chemistry, Physics, Astronomy, Geology</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@crashcourse/playlists\" target=\"_blank\">Crash Course</a></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Not a written source, but Crash Course is too useful for solving common knowledge gaps to not include</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Watch Crash Course while you're in line, waiting for someone, on hold, brushing your teeth, etc. Any time you could be scrolling on your phone, watch Crash Course instead.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Top Five LSAT Relevant Crash Course Sections</strong>: Intellectual Property (Ellen's favorite for LSAT students), Economics, US Government &amp; Politics, Art History, and Philosophy</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"pt-2\"><a href=\"/workouts-and-routines/workouts/extracurricular-reading\"><button class=\"\n    inline-flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-full\n    font-extrabold uppercase lh-outline\n    [transition:background-color_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),border-color_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),box-shadow_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),translate_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1)]\n    disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\n   \n          border-black text-black\n          hover:not-disabled:-translate-x-[3px]\n          hover:not-disabled:-translate-y-[3px]\n          hover:not-disabled:shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#171712]\n          active:not-disabled:-translate-x-[1px]\n          active:not-disabled:-translate-y-[1px]\n          active:not-disabled:shadow-[1px_1px_0_0_#171712]\n         h-[38px] gap-2 text-caption-medium border-[2px] pl-4 pr-3\">See full workout details<span class=\"flex items-center justify-center\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"12\" class=\"\" viewBox=\"0 0 26 19\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" data-testid=\"arrow-icon\"><path d=\"M20.25 10.9383H1.66667C1.19444 10.9383 0.798611 10.7786 0.479167 10.4592C0.159722 10.1397 0 9.74389 0 9.27167C0 8.79945 0.159722 8.40361 0.479167 8.08417C0.798611 7.76472 1.19444 7.605 1.66667 7.605H20.25L15.5 2.855C15.1667 2.52167 15.0069 2.13278 15.0208 1.